 health  symptoms but over time these kind of  came back or they got really worse and  typically some of these symptoms  included things like bloating  constipation IBS and other digestive  issues so let's start there so when  you're increasing  the amount of carbs in your diet which  for a lot of these youtubers they were  on like a high carb low fat vegan diet  when you're increasing the carbs you're  also inevitably usually gonna be  increasing the fiber fiber is great and  of course it's really important for  promoting regularity and most people are  not getting enough fiber in their diet  however an excessive fiber can also lead  to gut irritation bloating and otherwise  just like general digestive distress  there's also a substance called phytic  acid which tends to hang out in really  high fiber foods like beans nuts seeds  legumes typically although really great  vegan foods out there but the problem  with it is that it can also impair the  absorption of really important nutrients  like iron and zinc this typically isn't  a huge concern in generally healthy  balanced diets even vegan diets however  when you start to really restrict the  types of food that you're allowing  yourself to eat as we tend to see in  some of these really strict raw diets  you run the risk of serious mineral  deficiencies next let's talk about  amenorrhea which is loss of your  menstrual cycle and there's lots of  reasons why women lose their period and  strangely in a lot of the kind of high  high carb low fat raw vegan diet circles  this seems to be touted as a good thing  I can assure you folks it is not things  like weight loss under eating /  exercising stress and nutritional  deficiencies or common reasons why women  lose their period also a lot of these  high carb low fat vegan diets may  provide a lot of calories but they don't  provide enough of those healthy fats in  order to sustain women's fertility so  early research suggests that women who  follow a Mediterranean diet w