dy that should be  enough I think this just proves that  there isn't a one-size-fits-all model  when it comes to a healthy diet this is  really why intuitive eating is so  amazing and so important because it  comes down to listening to your body not  some set of arbitrary rules that some  youtubers set out only you are the  expert in your body a vegan diet might  feel really great to one person whereas  a high meat diet might feel great to  somebody else where something in between  might be great for another person and  those things may change just based on  the hour or the day or the week or the  month and that's okay other thing I want  to point out is that I think we can  actually make an impact and reap the  benefits of veganism without being so  extreme both for psychological and  physiological health I thought it was  really interesting what raw alignment  said in one of her videos where she said  that a lot of people cite huge huge  benefits when they go vegan which likely  also has a lot to do with the fact that  they've cut out a ton of processed foods  from a not so great diet so the jump  from one diet to the other one is quite  extreme but we can actually get a lot of  those same benefits simply by  incorporating more plant-based foods  into our diet and more Whole Foods into  our diet and then cutting back on some  of these processed foods that a lot of  us know are maybe not the greatest  the outcome here is threefold one we  reap the benefits of those plant-based  foods two we reduce our consumption of  these heavily processed less  nutrient-dense foods which we know of  course is going to also have an impact  on our health and three we play a role  in improving the animal welfare and also  the environment by reducing our overall  animal consumption I want everybody to  know that the abbeys kitchen channel is  a space for all people vegans and  non-vegans alike this is really where I  talk the latest no BS science with lots  of great information on we